    "old": "encoded with `var_to_bytes(dict)` (the form that does not encode objects)",
    "new": "var_to_bytes DOES encode an Object, as an EncodedObjectAsID (probed 2026-10-28); the defence is the bounded type walk rejecting TYPE_OBJECT plus the write-side VERIFYING decode and walk, not the encoder"
